"content_hash":"3968f60619dd7182fb9bbe187026c70a1020e864fb96e22580a824025c6d0f19","event_uuid":"3a09dd0c-509b-4b8f-8350-67befb3a11f3","position":{"commit_sha":"312c3dce71e173a7cb0182615ec795c7d1c63b11","position":"1786642554535686001-3a09dd0c-509b-4b8f-8350-67befb3a11f3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3e1b5c7614e96c16c165b625756714d5a507497802de672deb84f39cd3603b21","event_uuid":"31e87da0-c57c-467f-9127-4e6290f92b6c","position":{"commit_sha":"10679fbe6973522f666f190123a85e09328c781e","position":"1786642686240119001-31e87da0-c57c-467f-9127-4e6290f92b6c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f2e253ceccb4ffc045dc2253ee1084ff0b556b4b5bf05030e8134ecfe076e84e","event_uuid":"b3cec52f-baf7-4be6-a40c-bf8ab7c870f5","position":{"commit_sha":"fe88dd2d12242a10fe1b45dd5b0e8dcaff2d3488","position":"1786642875313396001-b3cec52f-baf7-4be6-a40c-bf8ab7c870f5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5ded179d7723495a3fa11ea38c356709a62a6b9ea35b35ea190f10776fe40a9d","event_uuid":"01b7d610-3707-4315-a09c-6d63d3461f38","position":{"commit_sha":"eb8dcdc8c50d40ea1c34fec38d7750f3b3bee88a","position":"1786645657946957001-01b7d610-3707-4315-a09c-6d63d3461f38"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OSS consensus audit (2026-08-13): APPROVED pattern.\n\nSetuptools states that sdist/wheel artifacts are stable for a test round, builds them once under a session lock, and exposes session-scoped readonly fixtures (pypa/setuptools@7d53128, setuptools/tests/fixtures.py#L70-L130). PyPA Build likewise builds a dependency wheel once in a session fixture for downstream tests (pypa/build@bf222f4, tests/test_projectbuilder.py#L427-L438).\n\nThis ticket's boundary is equally conservative: share only immutable clean inputs and identical prerequisite artifacts inside one pytest session; retain distinct real wheel-from-sdist, empty-env failure, sdist-content, and rebuild-from-sdist executions. Tracker cross-check: ducal-statuelike-ladybird requires those real boundaries but does not require rebuilding identical prerequisites per assertion. No rejection found.","timestamp":1786638514902213001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Repair evidence before Gerrit: baseline module 35.93s; final serial 12.25s (23.68s / 65.9% faster) and xdist -n2 12.27s. Held-out oracle /tmp/rebar_build_count_oracle.py was RED before repair (3 successful REBAR_BUILD_COMMIT=abc1234 prerequisite builds per worker/session), GREEN after repair (exactly 1; 7 passed), and RED again under a defect-seeded duplicate build (count 2). Corrupting the shared wheel's COMMIT returned the provenance assertion to RED (None != abc1234), then restoration returned GREEN. The fixture is session-scoped per worker, returns only immutable artifact paths, and consumers preserve distinct coverage: install-from-sdist still extracts locally and performs its env-unset rebuild; empty-env still performs a real failing build. No test, assertion, platform, Python version, coverage, or runner was removed; no new dependency. Lint/typecheck pass. Commit 8bdad57be7 carries the canonical ticket trailer. This matches Setuptools/PyPA's OSS practice of reusing immutable built artifacts within a test job.","timestamp":1786645657946957001}],"created_at":1786598923483139001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8d992c9e-a8b6-44d1-98ee-c4126cca8223","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ba7d-a412-bbc0-45cb"}],"description":"## Context and measured baseline\n\nThe real-artifact oracle from closed ticket ducal-statuelike-ladybird is valuable, but tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py independently runs git archive plus python -m build in four tests. On the current macOS host the unchanged module took 35.93s. Individually: install-from-sdist 8.40s, wheel-from-sdist 4.69s, sdist-content 4.53s, and empty-env failure 1.81s. Three tests repeat the identical successful clean-tree build with REBAR_BUILD_COMMIT=abc1234; install-from-sdist then performs a distinct second wheel build from the produced sdist.\n\n## OSS consensus and prior decisions\n\nSetuptools builds stable sdist/wheel artifacts once under a session lock and exposes session-scoped readonly fixtures (pypa/setuptools@7d53128, setuptools/tests/fixtures.py#L70-L130). PyPA Build builds a dependency wheel once in a session fixture for downstream tests (pypa/build@bf222f4, tests/test_projectbuilder.py#L427-L438). Closed ticket ducal-statuelike-ladybird requires the real wheel/sdist boundaries but does not require rebuilding an identical prerequisite per assertion. No rejection exists.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Change only tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py. Create one pytest session-scoped fixture per xdist worker using tmp_path_factory. It performs one git archive of HEAD and one real python -m build with REBAR_BUILD_COMMIT=abc1234.\n2. Return only immutable artifact paths from that fixture: the built wheel and sdist. Consumers inspect these archives read-only. No consumer receives the shared extracted source or output directory, preventing mutation of shared state.\n3. Wheel-from-sdist and sdist-content tests reuse the corresponding real shared artifacts while retaining their exact archive-content assertions.\n4. Install-from-sdist copies/extracts the shared sdist into its function-scoped tmp_path, then performs the distinct real env-unset rebuild there. Empty-env failure keeps its own function-scoped clean tree and real failing build because its environment and observable boundary differ.\n5. Strengthen the existing test module with deterministic build-call counting under a subprocess seam or equivalent fixture-level contract: one successful prerequisite build per pytest worker/session plus the retained empty-env and rebuild-from-sdist calls. Timing remains evidence, never a pass threshold.\n6. RED first against the current per-test rebuild behavior; hold the counter oracle out from the fixture refactor. GREEN, then seed both defects independently: restore a duplicate successful build and remove/corrupt COMMIT in the shared artifact. The counter/provenance oracles must return RED.\n7. Re-run the module serially and with xdist, report individual and total before/after durations, then run lint, typecheck, and the default pytest selection.\n\n## Test contract card\n\nauthoritative_contract: ducal-statuelike-ladybird and tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py require real wheel-from-sdist provenance, empty-env build failure, sdist build-info content, and env-unset rebuild-from-sdist preservation.\ntrigger_preconditions: a clean git archive without .git and REBAR_BUILD_COMMIT=abc1234; separate empty env and env-unset rebuild cases.\nproduction_path: python -m build through hatch_build.py, with real wheel/sdist archive inspection.\ntest_tier: real subprocess/package builds; a unit tier cannot prove artifact contents or the sdist-to-wheel boundary.\nobservable_postcondition: identical provenance/failure/content assertions; exactly one identical successful prerequisite build per worker/session, while empty-env failure and rebuild-from-sdist remain distinct real builds.\nnegative_control: empty-env failure does not consume the successful artifact; rebuild operates on a function-local extraction and cannot mutate shared inputs.\ncollateral_invariants: fixture lifetime ends with the pytest session; xdist workers share nothing; no cross-session/on-disk cache; no production file changes.\nci_gate: default pytest job and full Gerrit Verified gate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every existing real wheel/sdist assertion remains and still executes the relevant build boundary.\n- [ ] One successful clean-source prerequisite build is performed per pytest worker/session; identical prerequisite archive/build work is not repeated per test.\n- [ ] Shared consumers receive only read-only artifact paths; mutating extraction/rebuild work occurs in function-scoped copies.\n- [ ] A defect-seeded duplicate prerequisite build fails the deterministic call-count oracle, and a defect-seeded missing COMMIT still fails the provenance oracle.\n- [ ] Serial and xdist runs pass and report before/after individual durations; timing is evidence, never a gate.\n- [ ] Packaging tests remain hermetic, add no cross-session cache, and lint/typecheck/default pytest/Gerrit gates pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py","reason":"introduce a per-worker/session immutable real-artifact fixture and retain function-local distinct build boundaries with deterministic call-count coverage"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a0caabed-493c-4016-9a69-ff74723dbcb1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","performance","tests","packaging"],"ticket_id":"1c79-1d10-26b0-4a4e","ticket_type":"task","title":"Reuse build-provenance fixtures while preserving real wheel and sdist coverage","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9ceee607-4be4-49cc-8edb-da00488c77b6","8d992c9e-a8b6-44d1-98ee-c4126cca8223","21b6bdf7-3dbc-4d7d-b741-b8ed3d4f3edb","3b197b16-e5d3-41d0-b363-0a901094f93f","a0caabed-493c-4016-9a69-ff74723dbcb1","07df0d79-b764-4be2-9626-c9ac1ecde1ec","0ca03994-7841-43d1-8f6c-3a91efd5725e","3a09dd0c-509b-4b8f-8350-67befb3a11f3","31e87da0-c57c-467f-9127-4e6290f92b6c","b3cec52f-baf7-4be6-a40c-bf8ab7c870f5","01b7d610-3707-4315-a09c-6d63d3461f38"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786645657946957002,"uuid":"53e76506-5002-4d68-a9b9-0a749b57b9da"}